# Build outputs (rebuilt by scripts/install.ps1, never committed)
*.exe
*.disabled
bin/

# The portable release zip and its staging tree (scripts/package.ps1). These are
# release artifacts uploaded to GitHub, not source: the zip is ~5 MB of binaries
# that are rebuilt from the same source anyway, so committing it would only make
# the repository grow on every release.
dist/

# The packed plugin tarball (npm pack). It is a release asset, not source: it
# carries a vendored copy of the overlay, so committing it would add ~2 MB of
# binary per release. 73a9fad accidentally carried 1.2.11; do not repeat that.
packages/dsh-ai-terminal-pet/*.tgz

# Runtime / logs (machine-local state)
error.log
hang.log
*.tmp

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Backups
*.bak
*.bak-*

# Node artifacts (reporters use stdlib only, no node_modules needed)
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Local harness output
harness-out.json

# Agent working memory (machine-local, not project source)
.workbuddy-ai/
# Auto-dispatched task tickets from the personal KB hub. Machine-local, and the
# tickets are a template: docs/HANDOVER.md §34.6 records why they are not work.
.agents/

# Generated panel preview (see README: "Seeing a layout change without a window")
panel-preview.png

# Machine-local scratch: upstream registry snapshots, draft release notes, `npm pack`
# output and one-off probe scripts. Not project source; safe to delete at any time.
.local/

# The DSH plugin package ships a prebuilt overlay so `dsh plugin add` needs no
# Go toolchain. It is the one exception to the build-output rule above: it is
# a release artifact, not a local build. Regenerate it with `npm run vendor`
# (packages/dsh-ai-terminal-pet/scripts/vendor.mjs) after rebuilding bin/.
!packages/dsh-ai-terminal-pet/vendor/AI-Terminal-Pet.exe
